/*****************************************************************************
    shortCircuitT -- WHAT THE FOUR BOOLEAN SPELLINGS EVALUATE, counted.

    The TABLE is what an operator ANSWERS; SHORT-CIRCUIT is what it EVALUATES.
    Different questions, and only a COUNT can answer the second: a right arm
    that runs anyway still produces the right answer in most shapes.

    Every row counts fires of one side-effecting action, and the rows come in
    PAIRS -- one that must fire and one that must not -- because a zero on its
    own is what a right arm that never ran at all would also print.

    ⚠ FOUR ROWS, NOT EIGHT, SINCE THE WORD FORMS RETIRED 2026-09-10. It carried
    AND/OR rows too until `AND` and `OR` left incant/setup; the 2c scrub respelled
    their OPERATORS and left their LABELS, so four rows went on printing "AND" and
    "OR" while testing `&&` and `||` -- green, duplicated, and lying. Deleted
    rather than relabelled: two spellings of one operator is one row.

        SC-5  false && loud()     0    the skip
        SC-6  true  && loud()     1    its non-zero sibling
        SC-7  true  || loud()     0    the skip
        SC-8  false || loud()     1    its non-zero sibling

    ⚠ SC-7 IS THE ONE THAT WAS BROKEN. `||` carried the same operateMethod as
    `OR` and still evaluated its right arm, because TWO separate lists selected
    behaviour by SPELLING -- interpretXP's tier-3 binding and runShortCircuit's
    skip direction -- and neither knew the symbol. Both are registrations now.

    Header is prose on purpose -- bear-trap 27.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;

register(ShortCircuitT);
define
    sqT = 1;
    sqF = 0;
    sqFired;
    sqLoud code={ ++sqFired; return sqT; };
    sqRun code={
        sqFired = 0;   if sqF &&  sqLoud();   sqFired = sqFired;
        cerr "SC-5 false &&  loud  fires = " sqFired " (want 0)":;
        sqFired = 0;   if sqT &&  sqLoud();   sqFired = sqFired;
        cerr "SC-6 true  &&  loud  fires = " sqFired " (want 1)":;
        sqFired = 0;   if sqT ||  sqLoud();   sqFired = sqFired;
        cerr "SC-7 true  ||  loud  fires = " sqFired " (want 0 -- THE ONE THAT WAS BROKEN)":;
        sqFired = 0;   if sqF ||  sqLoud();   sqFired = sqFired;
        cerr "SC-8 false ||  loud  fires = " sqFired " (want 1)":;
        };
    ;
sqRun();
print "SHORTCIRCUIT SENTINEL -- reached the foot":;
stop();
